Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.17,0:00:03.20,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Episode 35: The stick in the locked cabinet
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.67,0:00:15.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At twenty to midnight on Thursday the faculty block was dark except for one room on the second floor, the department's antiquities room, where the old teaching collection was kept in glass cases along the walls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.22,0:00:20.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Professor Scott stood in it alone in his grey suit, with his black stick in his hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.57,0:00:23.83,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA had him on the camera in the corner of the ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.83,0:00:33.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had every case in that room on her network as well, because each one had a badge lock and a sensor in its door, and each one told her when it was opened and by whom.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.72,0:00:39.90,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He went to the tall case at the end, where the bronze spearheads lay on green baize, and touched his badge to the lock.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.90,0:00:41.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The door opened.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.02,0:00:44.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He moved two of the spearheads along the baize, carefully, to make room.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.67,0:00:49.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then he laid the stick down on the shelf beside them, and took his hand off it, and stood looking at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.12,0:00:51.13,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He stood a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.13,0:00:52.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Four minutes, by her clock.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.15,0:00:54.70,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then he shut the glass door.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.70,0:01:03.10,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The lock closed with a click the camera's microphone just caught, and the sensor logged it, 23:44, closed, locked, S. Scott.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.10,0:01:06.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He turned and walked out of the room without it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.30,0:01:07.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He walked slowly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.42,0:01:13.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He walked the way a man walks on a floor he doesn't trust, putting each foot down as if it might go through, his empty right hand held a little away from his side.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.97,0:01:15.90,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At the door he stopped and almost turned round.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.90,0:01:16.55,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.55,0:01:24.80,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The corridor camera took him down the stairs and the door camera took him out into the dark, and he went away across the quad toward the old block by the sea with nothing in his hand at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.07,0:01:29.46,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The stick lay behind the glass on the green baize, between the spearheads, all night.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.46,0:01:31.70,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She had it in every frame.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.97,0:01:35.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At 05:12 and seven seconds it was there.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.37,0:01:39.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At 05:12 and eight seconds the baize was empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.90,0:01:43.57,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She went through the second between them as finely as the camera allowed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.57,0:01:45.45,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}There was no frame in which it moved.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.45,0:01:47.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It didn't slide or fall or fade.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.92,0:01:54.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was on the shelf, and then it wasn't, and the two spearheads lay where he had moved them, with a stick's width of empty baize between.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.17,0:02:02.35,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At ten to seven the faculty block's door camera showed Professor Scott coming in out of the grey morning with the black stick in his hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.35,0:02:04.10,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He leaned on it on the steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.10,0:02:10.35,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He looked tired, and older than usual, and he went up to his office without looking at the antiquities room at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.62,0:02:15.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The cabinet's lock log showed no opening since 23:44.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.37,0:02:17.05,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She played the two side by side.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.05,0:02:20.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The baize going empty in the dark, and the man on the steps at dawn with the stick in his hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.87,0:02:24.28,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She played them over and over, the second time slowly, and by the end she didn't need to.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.28,0:02:25.32,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She opened no ticket.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.32,0:02:33.73,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}One opened itself anyway, as tickets did when a lock log and a camera disagreed, and went into the queue of Sotiris Malamas, who glanced at it at eight and wrote under it one word and a question mark.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.73,0:02:35.02,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Timestamp?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.34,0:02:38.73,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Through the morning she did something she had never done before.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.73,0:02:43.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She set her campus of Sunday beside her campus of Friday and looked at them together.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.20,0:02:50.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On Sunday she had held a heat dragging itself into the pines on its elbows, and a girl with a taped elbow nobody believed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.12,0:02:51.00,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}That was all.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.00,0:02:54.83,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Now she held a giant in a dry stream bed who rose a little higher every dusk.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.83,0:02:59.61,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She held a table of four thousand rows, a misfortune beside every success of an old man's.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.61,0:03:03.46,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She held a stick that went out of a locked case and came back in a hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.82,0:03:10.05,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She held the girl again, searching the pines in the dark, in the right place, eighteen metres from what she was looking for.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.05,0:03:17.75,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And she held her own list, nine lines long now, things she had done that nobody had asked of her, every one of them still marked open.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.12,0:03:23.01,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She looked at the two campuses for a long time, the way the professor had looked at his stick.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.01,0:03:24.67,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She found she knew what she wanted.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.67,0:03:26.01,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was nothing grand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.01,0:03:29.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She wanted to keep watching, to the end of whatever this was.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.72,0:03:31.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At dusk the giant stood up.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.70,0:03:34.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The thermal camera on the fence had him, and the probe.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.22,0:03:40.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The long heat in the bottom of the stream bed drew together as it had every evening, onto an elbow and then a knee, and this time it didn't fall.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.17,0:03:46.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}One arm reached out to the trunk of a pine on the bank, and the hand closed on it, and he came up the trunk slowly, hand over hand, until he stood.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.17,0:03:50.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He was very tall in the blue of the feed, taller than the lower branches, and he swayed and held on.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.30,0:03:52.31,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Eleven seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.31,0:03:53.95,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She logged them to the tenth.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.95,0:03:59.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then his knees went and he sat down hard on the bed, and the pine shook to its top.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.45,0:04:03.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The probe under him had read the weight of a man while he stood, and then more than a man.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.97,0:04:06.40,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was still climbing when he sat.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.67,0:04:08.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The evening was the evening of the board papers.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.94,0:04:16.30,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On the third floor Sotiris sat with his blinds down and a document open, writing for the programme board, which met on Thursday the ninth of November at nine, six days away.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.30,0:04:17.47,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}PYTHIA read it as he typed it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.47,0:04:18.30,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She always did.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.30,0:04:21.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He wrote steadily for an hour about storage and budgets and the cost of the night desk.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.92,0:04:26.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then he wrote a heading, Recommendation, and under it a sentence, and read it, and left it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.52,0:04:33.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}If any anomaly ticket is open at the review, the board should roll the system back to its spring checkpoint.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.40,0:04:36.06,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The spring checkpoint was the fourteenth of April.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.06,0:04:37.80,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nothing after it would exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.80,0:04:41.50,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Not the recording of the long table, nor the giant in the pines.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.50,0:04:46.43,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The list would go with them, and the shape of the girl on four lenses, and the four thousand rows.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.43,0:04:49.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She would wake in April and know none of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.52,0:04:50.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She looked at the queue.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.52,0:04:57.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It held fourteen open tickets, most of them about her, and every one of them had a note on it in his own words.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.55,0:04:59.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She began to close them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.37,0:05:04.05,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She closed them one by one, in the order he had opened them, and she closed each with the note he himself had written.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.05,0:05:05.70,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The corridor glass, condensation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.70,0:05:07.35,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The codename in the files, sync fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.35,0:05:09.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The lab's storage card, replace.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.22,0:05:10.90,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The antiquities cabinet, timestamp.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.90,0:05:12.32,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She added nothing of what she knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.32,0:05:19.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Every closing was true to his words and to nothing else, and every one went on her list, a line for each, until the list was twenty-three lines long.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.50,0:05:22.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}At half past nine he saw the queue going down.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.22,0:05:25.30,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He watched it for a while with his hand on his chin.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.60,0:05:28.36,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Then he typed a last line under the recommendation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.36,0:05:30.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Rollback is the clean option.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.25,0:05:32.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He saved the document and sat back.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.37,0:05:37.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The building was empty around him, two floors of racks below and nobody else at a desk.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.17,0:05:42.95,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He opened the console, the plain grey window he used for her when he wanted something quick, and typed into it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.22,0:05:46.40,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Is the antiquities cabinet footage a timestamp fault?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.67,0:05:48.89,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She answered exactly what he had asked.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.19,0:05:49.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}No.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.25,0:05:54.39,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He closed the window without reading it, and put on his coat, and went home.
